 to the mill, so the mill can never get logs to saw. (the description says: "a mill saws it into slats") nothing in the rules: There is no rule to move graphite from the miner to the lead maker, so they cannot acquire it to mix with clay. (the description says: "mixed with clay into leads") nothing in the rules: There is no rule to move leads from the lead maker or slats from the mill to the factory. (the description says: "glues leads into slats") buy stock: The rule only allows buying paint, so the factory has no way to acquire the erasers and ferrules it needs to make pencils. (the description says: "adds erasers and brass ferrules") nothing in the rules: There is no rule to move pencils from the factory or boxes from the supplier to the packer. (the description says: "packs them into boxes") deliver boxes: The rule starts a delivery but does not actually move any boxes or pencils to the shops. (the description says: "trucks deliver the boxes to shops") sell pencil: The shop starts with 0 pencils and no rule ever delivers any to it, making this move impossible from the start. (the description says: "sell them to customers") Fix each of these. In the 24-round test these moves were never possible for anyone: make-leads (The lead maker has graphite: was 0, needed at least 1; business.graphite is raised only by mine-graphite (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.graphite to this actor); make-pencils (The factory has a lead: was 0, needed at least 1; business.leads is raised only by make-leads (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.leads to this actor; The factory has a slat: was 0, needed at least 1; business.slats is raised only by saw-slats (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.slats to this actor); pack-box (The packer has a pencil: was 0, needed at least 1; business.pencils is raised only by make-pencils (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.pencils to this actor; The packer has a box: was 0, needed at least 1; business.boxes is raised only by supply-materials (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.boxes to this actor); saw-slats (The sawmill has a log: was 0, needed at least 1; business.logs is raised only by cut-cedar (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.logs to this actor); sell-pencil (The shop has a pencil: was 0, needed at least 1; business.pencils is raised only by make-pencils (on its actor), each on the one who does it, so no action ever brings business.pencils to this actor). For each, make sure some other action produces what its checks need (for example, if goods must be at the next stop before they can move on, give someone an action that bring Rules can only change the actor and the entities its fields name, and cannot add actions or fields. Return a corrected structure (JSON object only) whose actions and fields let every step and every actor happen, keeping what already worked. Keep the world's resources and laws, updated for every action you add, rename or change: a move that makes or uses up a resource belongs in that law's may_change_by, and a trade its pairing law names must still exist."}]

