[{"role": "system", "content": "You are proposing causal mechanics for a governed world model. Return exactly one JSON object and no prose or markdown. You are not writing code. mechanics must hold one mechanic for each of these moves: cut-cedar, send-logs-to-mill, saw-slats, send-slats-to-factory, mine-graphite, send-graphite-to-lead-maker, make-leads, send-leads-to-factory, supply-materials, send-paint-to-factory, send-erasers-to-factory, send-ferrules-to-factory, make-pencils, send-pencils-to-packer, send-boxes-to-packer, pack-box, send-boxes-to-truckers, deliver-boxes, sell-pencil; an empty mechanics list is always rejected. The response must satisfy response_contract. Every effect must be justified by represented state and the action description. Prefer conservative refusal checks over assumptions. Do not add reads/writes fields; the local compiler derives authority. Whenever you name a state path, copy it EXACTLY from allowed_state_paths. Where one change physically sets off another at once (a fall, a break, a spill, a noise heard nearby), write that consequence as a process with timing immediately."}, {"role": "user", "content": "{
